{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016McWDEJpXWJX93cHTvFKH1","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t// Store reads POSE artifacts from one project root (ADR-013: project-scoped).\n51\ttype Store struct {\n52\t\treviewView         *reviewOperationView\n53\t\treviewTime         *time.Time\n54\t\treviewReuse        *reviewReuseTraversal\n55\t\tonReviewVerify     func(scope string)\n56\t\tRoot               string // project root containing .pose/\n57\t\tFederatedProjectID string\n58\t\tFederatedResolver  *ArtifactResolver\n59\t\tdoctorCloseoutMemo *doctorCloseoutMemo\n60\t\tcloseoutTrace      *doctorCloseoutTrace\n61\t\t// closeoutChain is the chain of local aggregate scopes whose terminal\n62\t\t// verification is asking for this one, through their dependency edges:\n63\t\t// a scope already in it is a cycle and is not proven closed.\n64\t\tcloseoutChain []string\n65\t\t// indexMaterial marks the store computing an index's federated input\n66\t\t// material: an input of the index cannot depend on closeout state, which\n67\t\t// is derived from the index it binds (spec\n68\t\t// pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout).\n69\t\tindexMaterial bool\n70\t\t// specs, when set, is the spec listing of one operation, read once\n71\t\t// (spec pose-attention-within-a-second). Nil outside such an operation.\n72\t\tspecs *specSnapshot\n73\t\t// indexPin, when set, is the one index generation an operation reads from\n74\t\t// (spec pose-index-generation-integrity); see PinIndexes.\n75\t\tindexPin *IndexGenerationView\n76\t\t// FS is the filesystem of the operation this store serves (spec\n77\t\t// pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update D2): nil reads and writes\n78\t\t// the disk, a preview reads its staged view. A store built from this one\n79\t\t// carries it on.\n80\t\tFS Files\n81\t\t// planWithoutCloseoutGate builds a review plan without asking the\n82\t\t// closeout review gate, for the gate's own question about the plan's\n83\t\t// effective independence (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit).\n84\t\tplanWithoutCloseoutGate bool\n85\t}\n86\t\n87\t// fsys is the store's filesystem.\n88\tfunc (s Store) fsys() Files { return FilesOrNative(s.FS) }\n89\t\n90\t// specSnapshot holds one read of the specs directory. GetSpec lists every\n91\t// spec to find one, and the obligation producers call it per spec, so a\n92\t// projection read every spec file once per spec per producer.\n93\ttype specSnapshot struct {\n94\t\tonce  sync.Once\n95\t\tspecs []Spec\n96\t\terr   error\n97\t\t// bundleScopes maps a review bundle file to the scope its payload names,\n98\t\t// read once per operation; ListReviewBundles otherwise decodes every\n99\t\t// bundle for every scoped call.\n100\t\tbundleScopes sync.Map\n101\t\t// transfers is the listing of the project's transfer plans, read once per operation\n102\t\t// (spec pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once).\n103\t\ttransfersOnce sync.Once\n104\t\ttransfers     transferListing\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\t// bundleScope returns the scope ref of the bundle file name in dir, reading\n108\t// it on first use. An unreadable bundle has no scope and matches nothing.\n109\tfunc (snapshot *specSnapshot) bundleScope(dir, name string) string {\n110\t\tif scope, ok := snapshot.bundleScopes.Load(name); ok {\n111\t\t\treturn scope.(string)\n112\t\t}\n113\t\tscope := \"\"\n114\t\tif raw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, name)); err == nil {\n115\t\t\tvar header struct {\n116\t\t\t\tPayload struct {\n117\t\t\t\t\tScope struct {\n118\t\t\t\t\t\tRef string `json:\"ref\"`\n119\t\t\t\t\t} `json:\"scope\"`\n120\t\t\t\t} `json:\"payload\"`\n121\t\t\t}\n122\t\t\tif json.Unmarshal(raw, &header) == nil {\n123\t\t\t\tscope = header.Payload.Scope.Ref\n124\t\t\t}\n125\t\t}\n126\t\tsnapshot.bundleScopes.Store(name, scope)\n127\t\treturn scope\n128\t}\n129\t\n130\t// withSpecSnapshot returns a store whose spec listing is read once and reused\n131\t// for the rest of the operation. Specs do not change during one read.\n132\tfunc (s Store) withSpecSnapshot() Store {\n133\t\ts.specs = &specSnapshot{}\n134\t\treturn s\n135\t}\n136\t\n137\t// cloneSpec copies the slices so no caller can change another's spec.\n138\tfunc cloneSpec(sp Spec) Spec {\n139\t\tclone := func(values []string) []string {\n140\t\t\tif values == nil {\n141\t\t\t\treturn nil\n142\t\t\t}\n143\t\t\treturn append(make([]string, 0, len(values)), values...)\n144\t\t}\n145\t\tsp.DependsOn = clone(sp.DependsOn)\n146\t\tsp.Remediates = clone(sp.Remediates)\n147\t\tsp.Components = clone(sp.Components)\n148\t\tsp.Delivers = clone(sp.Delivers)\n149\t\tif sp.Priority != nil {\n150\t\t\tpriority := *sp.Priority\n151\t\t\tsp.Priority = &priority\n152\t\t}\n153\t\treturn sp\n154\t}\n155\t\n156\tfunc (s Store) specsDir() string { return filepath.Join(s.Root, \".pose\", \"specs\") }\n157\t\n158\t// GetSpec returns a spec by slug, body included. The canonical layout is\n159\t// .pose/specs/<slug>/spec.md or date-prefixed .pose/specs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>/spec.md;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"9dd71247-3724-4749-9e2d-ce7f1fdb0d19","timestamp":"2026-11-18T04:00:10.749Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/p5.72rW0j/pose-review-run-3323286775/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go","content":"// Store reads POSE artifacts from one project root (ADR-013: project-scoped).\ntype Store struct {\n\treviewView         *reviewOperationView\n\treviewTime         *time.Time\n\treviewReuse        *reviewReuseTraversal\n\tonReviewVerify     func(scope string)\n\tRoot               string // project root containing .pose/\n\tFederatedProjectID string\n\tFederatedResolver  *ArtifactResolver\n\tdoctorCloseoutMemo *doctorCloseoutMemo\n\tcloseoutTrace      *doctorCloseoutTrace\n\t// closeoutChain is the chain of local aggregate scopes whose terminal\n\t// verification is asking for this one, through their dependency edges:\n\t// a scope already in it is a cycle and is not proven closed.\n\tcloseoutChain []string\n\t// indexMaterial marks the store computing an index's federated input\n\t// material: an input of the index cannot depend on closeout state, which\n\t// is derived from the index it binds (spec\n\t// pose-index-material-does-not-ask-closeout).\n\tindexMaterial bool\n\t// specs, when set, is the spec listing of one operation, read once\n\t// (spec pose-attention-within-a-second). Nil outside such an operation.\n\tspecs *specSnapshot\n\t// indexPin, when set, is the one index generation an operation reads from\n\t// (spec pose-index-generation-integrity); see PinIndexes.\n\tindexPin *IndexGenerationView\n\t// FS is the filesystem of the operation this store serves (spec\n\t// pose-update-dry-run-reports-the-whole-update D2): nil reads and writes\n\t// the disk, a preview reads its staged view. A store built from this one\n\t// carries it on.\n\tFS Files\n\t// planWithoutCloseoutGate builds a review plan without asking the\n\t// closeout review gate, for the gate's own question about the plan's\n\t// effective independence (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit).\n\tplanWithoutCloseoutGate bool\n}\n\n// fsys is the store's filesystem.\nfunc (s Store) fsys() Files { return FilesOrNative(s.FS) }\n\n// specSnapshot holds one read of the specs directory. GetSpec lists every\n// spec to find one, and the obligation producers call it per spec, so a\n// projection read every spec file once per spec per producer.\ntype specSnapshot struct {\n\tonce  sync.Once\n\tspecs []Spec\n\terr   error\n\t// bundleScopes maps a review bundle file to the scope its payload names,\n\t// read once per operation; ListReviewBundles otherwise decodes every\n\t// bundle for every scoped call.\n\tbundleScopes sync.Map\n\t// transfers is the listing of the project's transfer plans, read once per operation\n\t// (spec pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once).\n\ttransfersOnce sync.Once\n\ttransfers     transferListing\n}\n\n// bundleScope returns the scope ref of the bundle file name in dir, reading\n// it on first use. An unreadable bundle has no scope and matches nothing.\nfunc (snapshot *specSnapshot) bundleScope(dir, name string) string {\n\tif scope, ok := snapshot.bundleScopes.Load(name); ok {\n\t\treturn scope.(string)\n\t}\n\tscope := \"\"\n\tif raw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, name)); err == nil {\n\t\tvar header struct {\n\t\t\tPayload struct {\n\t\t\t\tScope struct {\n\t\t\t\t\tRef string `json:\"ref\"`\n\t\t\t\t} `json:\"scope\"`\n\t\t\t} `json:\"payload\"`\n\t\t}\n\t\tif json.Unmarshal(raw, &header) == nil {\n\t\t\tscope = header.Payload.Scope.Ref\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tsnapshot.bundleScopes.Store(name, scope)\n\treturn scope\n}\n\n// withSpecSnapshot returns a store whose spec listing is read once and reused\n// for the rest of the operation. Specs do not change during one read.\nfunc (s Store) withSpecSnapshot() Store {\n\ts.specs = &specSnapshot{}\n\treturn s\n}\n\n// cloneSpec copies the slices so no caller can change another's spec.\nfunc cloneSpec(sp Spec) Spec {\n\tclone := func(values []string) []string {\n\t\tif values == nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn append(make([]string, 0, len(values)), values...)\n\t}\n\tsp.DependsOn = clone(sp.DependsOn)\n\tsp.Remediates = clone(sp.Remediates)\n\tsp.Components = clone(sp.Components)\n\tsp.Delivers = clone(sp.Delivers)\n\tif sp.Priority != nil {\n\t\tpriority := *sp.Priority\n\t\tsp.Priority = &priority\n\t}\n\treturn sp\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) specsDir() string { return filepath.Join(s.Root, \".pose\", \"specs\") }\n\n// GetSpec returns a spec by slug, body included. The canonical layout is\n// .pose/specs/<slug>/spec.md or date-prefixed .pose/specs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>/spec.md;","numLines":110,"startLine":50,"totalLines":711}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016McWDEJpXWJX93cHTvFKH1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
