{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch9mvBZSUivmzfwUu7MLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: approved\n\n# Review: spec:pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation\n\nI recommend approving. The implementation matches R1–R6 and D1–D2. I found two low-severity gaps in the tests and recorded both as follow-ups. Neither is a correctness defect.\n\nOne thing first: **my own run of `pose validate --strict` (both module and full) exited 1** in this sandbox. The same 11 checks failed in both runs, and none of them is related to this change:\n- **`/var/tmp` ownership:** \"/var/tmp belongs to another user\" broke the delegate, detach and run-continuity checks.\n- **Network:** `curl` got a 403 from the published-release listing (install journeys).\n- **Runtime host:** it couldn't start, which broke `runtime-qos` and `resident-cache`. `worktreeruntime` timed out at 600 s.\n- **Sandbox chmod:** `operation_files_test.go:584` failed on a file-mode change.\n\nNone of these checks covers the changed files. The new check `doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration` and the `build` check passed in my run, and the sealed bundle records every one of the failing checks as passing. So for both `validate` tools I cite the sealed evidence and note the local exit 1 in the rationale.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Diff, read in full:** `doctor_closeout_memo.go`, `closeout_review_policy.go` (+40), `review_operation_view.go` (+10), `governance_read_view.go` (+4), `spec.go` (+7).\n- **Memo soundness:**\n  - Only approvals are kept. Results that are false, errors, cycle cuts, project crossings, and traces past their limits all cut the parent trace.\n  - A cached result is reused only when nothing in the current ancestor chain overlaps the scopes that evaluation visited. That is enough, because `closeoutChain` is read only in `localScopeClosed` (`closeout_review_policy.go:393`).\n  - Removing the append from `localScopeClosed` changes nothing, because `computeClosedByReceipt:781` adds the same element.\n- **Context isolation:**\n  - The key uses root and project from the bound view.\n  - Reuse is refused when the clock, view, resolver, Authorize callback, `indexMaterial` or `planWithoutCloseoutGate` differ, or once the read view is finalized.\n  - Both view constructors clear the memo and trace (`governance_read_view.go:2594,2612`).\n  - Remote stores have no memo, so they fall back and cut.\n- **Error precedence:** in `CloseoutReviewsOwed` (`closeout_review_policy.go:888-899`), if the query returns an error or the final audit fails, no list is returned. Doctor shows that as a `closeout-review.owed` warning with the error text and a fix (`cli/doctor.go:1616-1619`).\n- **Commands I ran:**\n  - `go build ./...` and `go vet ./internal/pose`: clean.\n  - `go test -race ./internal/pose -run 'TestDoctorResolverCatalogue|DoctorCloseoutMemo|Doctor'`: pass, 12/12 new tests.\n  - `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'ReviewOperationView|ReviewScopeOperation|CloseoutReviewPolicy|Doctor'`: `pose` passes. `cli` has one failure, `TestRunContinuityDoctorStatusAndPending`, caused by the `/var/tmp` ownership check in `delegation_task.go:434`, which this change doesn't touch.\n  - `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`: exit 0. 10 claims, 24 observed paths, and 978 orphan warnings about paths elsewhere in the repo.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` exited 0, and the `go-build*` removal under `GOTMPDIR` exited 0 with none left.\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| backend-concurrency | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration (`-race`) |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-outcomes-v2-contract |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration |\n| correctness | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration |\n| documentation | passed | structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0 |\n| operability | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration |\n| requirements | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0 |\n| security | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration |\n\n## Defects\n\n- **F1 (low): `pose-mcp/internal/pose/doctor_closeout_memo_test.go:158`.** The check that a store with a different clock stays out of the memo asserts `computes == 0`. But `onCompute` only fires when the memo misses, so a wrong memo hit would also give 0 (and `closed == true`). The test can't catch the regression it names.\n- **F2 (low): `pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:879-899`.** No test calls the public `CloseoutReviewsOwed` on a current (versioned) index and checks that a failed final audit returns no list (R1). The memo tests use legacy-index fixtures and call `WithReviewOperationView` plus `withDoctorCloseoutMemo` directly, while the existing public-API tests take the legacy branch.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/doctor_closeout_memo_test.go\",\n      \"line\": 158,\n      \"summary\": \"Clock-isolation assertion (computes == 0) cannot distinguish the correct bypass from an incorrect memo hit, since onCompute fires only on memo miss and both paths return closed=true; the test does not detect the regression it names.\",\n      \"action\": \"Assert non-entry directly (e.g. count computeClosedByReceipt invocations via a hook on the bypass path, or poison the cached entry and require a recomputed result) for the different-clock store.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-18\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 888,\n      \"summary\": \"R1 negative path lacks direct evidence: no test drives the public CloseoutReviewsOwed on a current (versioned) index and shows a failed final audit yields an error and no list; memo tests use legacy fixtures and call the internal composition, existing public tests take the legacy branch.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add a test that publishes an index generation, mutates a captured input during CloseoutReviewsOwed, and asserts (nil, ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged); and one asserting the legacy branch still lists.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-18\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Memo and trace are mutex-guarded, no lock is held across recursive verification (doctor_closeout_memo.go:170), memo is closed in a defer at callback exit and cleared by both view constructors; focused tests pass under -race locally.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-outcomes-v2-contract\", \"rationale\": \"No exported signature, JSON shape or CLI/MCP output changed; new Store fields and the specCatalogueListed hook are unexported.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Errors and false results are never cached (TestDoctorCloseoutMemoErrorsAndRemoteBoundary); query error takes precedence, then audit error, and no list is returned on either.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Resolver snapshots are allocated after withGovernanceReadView and before the binding pointer is fixed, in both the operation and scope-operation entries; remote crossings remain unmemoized and cut the parent trace.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Audit/binding failures surface through doctor's closeout-review.owed warn with the error text and a remediation (cli/doctor.go:1616-1619); no sensitive data added.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the public CloseoutReviewsOwed and doctor caller: legacy-unversioned instances keep the prior advisory path verbatim; versioned instances now fail closed on audit failure as R1 requires. No public CLI/file/MCP contract changed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Reviewed memo soundness: approvals reused only when the ancestor chain is disjoint from the visited scopes, which suffices because closeoutChain is only consulted in localScopeClosed; equivalence with the plain verifier is asserted for linear, ancestor-intersecting and cyclic topologies.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Examined doctor output, help and templates: no user-visible behavior or scaffold changed; the spec documents approach, decisions, known gaps and that F5 remains open; code comments explain memo lifetime and cut rules.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Doctor still reports a failure to list owed reviews as an actionable warn naming pose closeout-check; memo limits fall back to the original verifier rather than erroring.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R2/R4/R5 covered by TestDoctorResolverCatalogue*, R3 by PreservesResolution, R6 by TestDoctorCloseoutMemo*; R1 is implemented but its public-path negative test is weak (F2, accepted low follow-up).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec's Artifacts list and non-goals: only the declared files changed, no persistent cache, catalogue or policy change, memo confined to the CloseoutReviewsOwed callback per D1/D2.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined authority boundaries: a dynamic Authorize callback disables the memo; unauthorized/missing/duplicate identities resolve identically to the live path; snapshots never cross operations; final audit still refuses changed inputs including same-size/restored-mtime edits.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; 10 claims, 24 observed; 978 warnings are orphan paths elsewhere in the repo.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; relied on the sealed structure evidence and direct code reading instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; component surface reviewed directly via the diff.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; integration impact judged from sealed integration evidence and code reading.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; not needed to judge this bugfix scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; review targets were taken from the sealed change set.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed evidence passes. My sandboxed re-run of pose validate --strict exited 1 on 11 environment-bound checks (/var/tmp ownership refusals, release-listing HTTP 403, runtime host start, chmod); none exercises the changed files.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed evidence passes; in my re-run of pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp the scope's own check and build passed, while the same 11 environment-bound checks failed (exit 1) for sandbox reasons unrelated to this change.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":78946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":515},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"0bfd06da-9f72-4fee-a3f4-e3f06081df9c","timestamp":"2026-11-18T04:39:02.692Z","request_id":"req_011Ch9mvBLJPC82xwbZF9sfx"}
{"duration_api_ms":243032,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":1.3816178,"usage":{"input_tokens":68,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74551,"cache_read_input_tokens":1831189,"output_tokens":20935,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7408},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74551,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6459,"cache_read_input_tokens":78946,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":515},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":68,"outputTokens":20935,"cacheReadInputTokens":1831189,"cacheCreationInputTokens":74551,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3816178,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7408,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":74551,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":38,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"decision: approved\n\n# Review: spec:pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation\n\nI recommend approving. The implementation matches R1–R6 and D1–D2. I found two low-severity gaps in the tests and recorded both as follow-ups. Neither is a correctness defect.\n\nOne thing first: **my own run of `pose validate --strict` (both module and full) exited 1** in this sandbox. The same 11 checks failed in both runs, and none of them is related to this change:\n- **`/var/tmp` ownership:** \"/var/tmp belongs to another user\" broke the delegate, detach and run-continuity checks.\n- **Network:** `curl` got a 403 from the published-release listing (install journeys).\n- **Runtime host:** it couldn't start, which broke `runtime-qos` and `resident-cache`. `worktreeruntime` timed out at 600 s.\n- **Sandbox chmod:** `operation_files_test.go:584` failed on a file-mode change.\n\nNone of these checks covers the changed files. The new check `doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration` and the `build` check passed in my run, and the sealed bundle records every one of the failing checks as passing. So for both `validate` tools I cite the sealed evidence and note the local exit 1 in the rationale.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Diff, read in full:** `doctor_closeout_memo.go`, `closeout_review_policy.go` (+40), `review_operation_view.go` (+10), `governance_read_view.go` (+4), `spec.go` (+7).\n- **Memo soundness:**\n  - Only approvals are kept. Results that are false, errors, cycle cuts, project crossings, and traces past their limits all cut the parent trace.\n  - A cached result is reused only when nothing in the current ancestor chain overlaps the scopes that evaluation visited. That is enough, because `closeoutChain` is read only in `localScopeClosed` (`closeout_review_policy.go:393`).\n  - Removing the append from `localScopeClosed` changes nothing, because `computeClosedByReceipt:781` adds the same element.\n- **Context isolation:**\n  - The key uses root and project from the bound view.\n  - Reuse is refused when the clock, view, resolver, Authorize callback, `indexMaterial` or `planWithoutCloseoutGate` differ, or once the read view is finalized.\n  - Both view constructors clear the memo and trace (`governance_read_view.go:2594,2612`).\n  - Remote stores have no memo, so they fall back and cut.\n- **Error precedence:** in `CloseoutReviewsOwed` (`closeout_review_policy.go:888-899`), if the query returns an error or the final audit fails, no list is returned. Doctor shows that as a `closeout-review.owed` warning with the error text and a fix (`cli/doctor.go:1616-1619`).\n- **Commands I ran:**\n  - `go build ./...` and `go vet ./internal/pose`: clean.\n  - `go test -race ./internal/pose -run 'TestDoctorResolverCatalogue|DoctorCloseoutMemo|Doctor'`: pass, 12/12 new tests.\n  - `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'ReviewOperationView|ReviewScopeOperation|CloseoutReviewPolicy|Doctor'`: `pose` passes. `cli` has one failure, `TestRunContinuityDoctorStatusAndPending`, caused by the `/var/tmp` ownership check in `delegation_task.go:434`, which this change doesn't touch.\n  - `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`: exit 0. 10 claims, 24 observed paths, and 978 orphan warnings about paths elsewhere in the repo.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` exited 0, and the `go-build*` removal under `GOTMPDIR` exited 0 with none left.\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| backend-concurrency | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration (`-race`) |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-outcomes-v2-contract |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration |\n| backend-observability | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration |\n| correctness | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration |\n| documentation | passed | structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0 |\n| operability | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration |\n| requirements | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0 |\n| security | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration |\n\n## Defects\n\n- **F1 (low): `pose-mcp/internal/pose/doctor_closeout_memo_test.go:158`.** The check that a store with a different clock stays out of the memo asserts `computes == 0`. But `onCompute` only fires when the memo misses, so a wrong memo hit would also give 0 (and `closed == true`). The test can't catch the regression it names.\n- **F2 (low): `pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:879-899`.** No test calls the public `CloseoutReviewsOwed` on a current (versioned) index and checks that a failed final audit returns no list (R1). The memo tests use legacy-index fixtures and call `WithReviewOperationView` plus `withDoctorCloseoutMemo` directly, while the existing public-API tests take the legacy branch.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/doctor_closeout_memo_test.go\",\n      \"line\": 158,\n      \"summary\": \"Clock-isolation assertion (computes == 0) cannot distinguish the correct bypass from an incorrect memo hit, since onCompute fires only on memo miss and both paths return closed=true; the test does not detect the regression it names.\",\n      \"action\": \"Assert non-entry directly (e.g. count computeClosedByReceipt invocations via a hook on the bypass path, or poison the cached entry and require a recomputed result) for the different-clock store.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-18\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\",\n      \"line\": 888,\n      \"summary\": \"R1 negative path lacks direct evidence: no test drives the public CloseoutReviewsOwed on a current (versioned) index and shows a failed final audit yields an error and no list; memo tests use legacy fixtures and call the internal composition, existing public tests take the legacy branch.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add a test that publishes an index generation, mutates a captured input during CloseoutReviewsOwed, and asserts (nil, ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged); and one asserting the legacy branch still lists.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-18\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Memo and trace are mutex-guarded, no lock is held across recursive verification (doctor_closeout_memo.go:170), memo is closed in a defer at callback exit and cleared by both view constructors; focused tests pass under -race locally.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-outcomes-v2-contract\", \"rationale\": \"No exported signature, JSON shape or CLI/MCP output changed; new Store fields and the specCatalogueListed hook are unexported.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Errors and false results are never cached (TestDoctorCloseoutMemoErrorsAndRemoteBoundary); query error takes precedence, then audit error, and no list is returned on either.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Resolver snapshots are allocated after withGovernanceReadView and before the binding pointer is fixed, in both the operation and scope-operation entries; remote crossings remain unmemoized and cut the parent trace.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Audit/binding failures surface through doctor's closeout-review.owed warn with the error text and a remediation (cli/doctor.go:1616-1619); no sensitive data added.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the public CloseoutReviewsOwed and doctor caller: legacy-unversioned instances keep the prior advisory path verbatim; versioned instances now fail closed on audit failure as R1 requires. No public CLI/file/MCP contract changed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Reviewed memo soundness: approvals reused only when the ancestor chain is disjoint from the visited scopes, which suffices because closeoutChain is only consulted in localScopeClosed; equivalence with the plain verifier is asserted for linear, ancestor-intersecting and cyclic topologies.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Examined doctor output, help and templates: no user-visible behavior or scaffold changed; the spec documents approach, decisions, known gaps and that F5 remains open; code comments explain memo lifetime and cut rules.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Doctor still reports a failure to list owed reviews as an actionable warn naming pose closeout-check; memo limits fall back to the original verifier rather than erroring.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R2/R4/R5 covered by TestDoctorResolverCatalogue*, R3 by PreservesResolution, R6 by TestDoctorCloseoutMemo*; R1 is implemented but its public-path negative test is weak (F2, accepted low follow-up).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-30a434e2df6ef2a0\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec's Artifacts list and non-goals: only the declared files changed, no persistent cache, catalogue or policy change, memo confined to the CloseoutReviewsOwed callback per D1/D2.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined authority boundaries: a dynamic Authorize callback disables the memo; unauthorized/missing/duplicate identities resolve identically to the live path; snapshots never cross operations; final audit still refuses changed inputs including same-size/restored-mtime edits.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-asks-every-closeout-in-one-operation --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; 10 claims, 24 observed; 978 warnings are orphan paths elsewhere in the repo.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; relied on the sealed structure evidence and direct code reading instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; component surface reviewed directly via the diff.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; integration impact judged from sealed integration evidence and code reading.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; not needed to judge this bugfix scope.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; review targets were taken from the sealed change set.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed evidence passes. My sandboxed re-run of pose validate --strict exited 1 on 11 environment-bound checks (/var/tmp ownership refusals, release-listing HTTP 403, runtime host start, chmod); none exercises the changed files.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-federated-spec-capture-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed evidence passes; in my re-run of pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp the scope's own check and build passed, while the same 11 environment-bound checks failed (exit 1) for sandbox reasons unrelated to this change.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":2143,"type":"result","duration_ms":2375951,"uuid":"12e7c547-5c1a-4df7-a648-411249da9193","ttft_stream_ms":2047,"time_to_request_ms":145,"first_content_frame_ms":2048,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":68,"outputTokens":20935,"cacheReadInputTokens":1831189,"cacheCreationInputTokens":74551,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3816178,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7408,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":74551,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-1